  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday) \nIssued at 1113 AM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nTo start the long term period, we will be in the nicest airmass \nwe've had so far this summer. Dew points on Thursday will be in the \nlow to mid 60s with highs in the low to mid 80s. Friday will be \nsimilar but a couple degrees warmer. A shortwave will ride northwest \nupper flow and approach the area Friday night into Saturday which \nwill reintroduce some low to medium rain chances. Temperatures will \ncreep up over the weekend with the possibility of a couple more \nshortwaves bringing additional storm storms chances going into early \nnext week. There is some uncertainty of how far east ridging \ninfluences pushes which will affect our rain chances and \ntemperatures next week.",
